 "MY-H1007": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1007",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1)  These regulations may be cited as the Petroleum (Income Tax)\n(Marginal Field) Regulations 2013.\n\n(2)  These Regulations are deemed to have come into operation on\n30 November 2010.\n\nApplication"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  These Regulations shall apply to all chargeable persons carrying on petroleum\noperations in a marginal field.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. For the purposes of these Regulations—\n\n \"marginal field\" means a field in a petroleum a greement area as provided for\nunder regulation 4.\n\nMarginal field"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The Minister  may determine a m arginal field  which is a field in a petroleum\nagreement area which has potential crude oil reserves not exceeding thirty million stock\ntank barrels or natural gas reserves not exceeding five hundred billion standard cubic\nfeet.\n\nGross income"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5.  (1)  In ascertaining t he gross income of a chargeable person from his\npetroleum operations carried on under a petroleum agreement, income from petroleum\n\noperations in a marginal field of that chargeable person shall be treated separately from\nhis other petroleum operations.\n\n (2)  Where the chargeable person carries on petroleum operations in two or\nmore marginal fields under a petr oleum agreement, income from all  those marginal\nfields shall be taken as the total gross income of  that chargeable person from all  those\nfields.\n\nAdjusted income"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "6. The adjusted income  of a chargeable person for the basis period for a year of\nassessment from his petroleum operations in  a marginal field shall be an amount\nascertained in accordance with Part III Chapter 3 of the Act.\nAdjusted loss"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "7. (1) Where but, for an insufficiency of gross income of a chargeable person for\nthe basis period for a year of assessment from his petrole um operations in marginal\nfield, there would have been an amount of adjusted income of that ch argeable person\nfor that period, the amount by which the total of all such deductions as would then have\nbeen allowed under Part III Chapter 3 of the Act in ascertaining that adjusted income\nexceeds his gross income for that period from his petroleum operations in that marginal\nfield shall be taken to be the amount of his adjusted loss for that period from that\npetroleum operations.\n\n(2)  The adjusted loss as certained under subregulation ( 1) shall only be\nallowed as a deduction against the statutory income of the chargeable person fr om his\npetroleum operations in a marginal field.\nStatutory income"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 8,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 8"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "8. Subject to regulations 9 and 10 , the statutory income of a chargeable person for\nthe basis period for a year of assessment in respect of petroleum operations in a\nmarginal field shall be  ascertained in accordance with Chapter 4 Part III of the Act and\nthe Petroleum (Income Tax) (Accelerated Capital Allowance) (Marginal Field) Rules\n2013 [P.U. (A) 119/2013].\n\nUnabsorbed capital allowance"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 9,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 9"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "9. Where, by reason of the absence or insufficiency of the adjusted income of a\nchargeable person from his petroleum operations in a marginal field for the basis period\nfor a year of assessment, effect cannot be given or cannot be given in full to the\nallowance as determined to which the chargeable perso n is entitled under regulation 8\nfor that year of assessment, then so much of that allowance which cannot be made shall\nbe made in the first subsequent year of assessment for the basis period for which there\nis adjusted income from petroleum operations in  a marginal field, and for subsequent\nyears of assessment until the whole of the allowance to which he is so entitled is made.\n\nAssessable income"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 10,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 10"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "10. (1)  The assessable income of a chargeable person from petroleum operations\nin a marginal field for a year of  assessment (in this regulation referred to as \"the\nrelevant year\") shall consist of the amount of his statutory income for the relevant year\nfrom that petroleum operations in a marginal field reduced by the amount of any\nadjusted loss from that petroleum operations for the basis period for the year of\nassessment preceding the relevant year of assessment which has not been deducted\nfrom his statutory income from that petroleum operations for a year of assessment\nprior to the relevant year.\n\n(2)  A deduction of any adjusted loss under subregulation (1) shall be made as\nfar as possible from the statutory income of the chargeable person from his petroleum\noperations in a marginal field for the first year of assessment after that for the basis\nperiod for which t hat loss is the adjusted loss, and, so far as it cannot be so made, then\nfrom the statutory income from that petroleum operations for the next year of\nassessment, and so on.\n\n(3) The assessable income ascertained under subregulation (1) shall be\ntreated as part of the chargeable income of a chargeable person for a year of assessment\nfor the purpose of section 22 of the Act.\n\nChargeable income"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 11,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 11"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "11.  Subject to  section 22 of the Act,  the  chargeable income of a chargeable person\nfrom petroleum operations i n a marginal field for a year of assessment\n(in this regulation referred to as \"the relevant year\") shall consist of the amount of his\nassessable income for the relevant year from that petroleum operations in a marginal\nfield reduced by an amount equal to any gift of money or the cost of contribution or\nvalue of contribution made by that chargeable person in a basis period for that year of\nassessment shall be determined in accordance with the following formula:\n    A x C\n    B\nwhere          A is the gross income of the chargeable person from a\nmarginal field;\n                     B  is the total gross income of the chargeable person\nfrom petroleum operations; and\n                     C  is the gift of money or the c ost of contribution or\nvalue of contribution made  by that chargeable\nperson in the basis period  for that year of\nassessment.\n\nSeparate account"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 12,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 12"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "12. A chargeable person shall maintain separate account s for his income derived\nfrom a marginal field and for his income derived from other petroleum operations.\n\nMade 22 March 2013\n[Perb. CR(8.09)681/2 -61(Sj.19) Jld. 3(Sk.2); LHDN. 01/35/(S)/42/51 Klt. 17;\nPN(PU2)80A/XVI]\n\nTAN SRI DR. MOHD SHUKOR BIN MAHFAR\nDirector General of Inland Revenue"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
