 "MY-H1076": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1076",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1.  (1)  This order may be cited as the Capital Markets and Services\n(Prescription of Securities and Islamic Securities)  (Investment Note and Islamic\nInvestment Note) Order 2016.\n\n(2)  This Order comes into operation on 16 May 2016.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  In this Order—\n\n\"investment note\" means any contract, agreement, note or other document\nevidencing a monetary loan, executed or offered, on or through an electronic platform,\nwhere an investor expects a financial return, but does not include—\n\n(a) any right, option or interest in respect of such contract, agreement, note\nor other document;\n\n(b) a cheque, banker's draft or any other bill of exchange or a letter of credit;\n\n(c) a banknote, guarantee or an insurance policy; or\n\n(d) a statement, passbook or other document showing any balance in a\ncurrent, deposit or savings account;\n\n\"Islamic investment note\" means any contract, agreement, note or other\ndocument evidencing undivided ownership or investment in any assets in compliance\nwith Shariah principles endorsed by Shariah Advisory Council, and is executed or\noffered, on or through an electronic platform , where an investor expects a financial\nreturn, but does not include—\n\n(a) any right, option or interest in respect of such contract, agreement, note\nor other document;\n\n(b) a cheque, banker's draft or any other bill of exchange or a letter of credit;\n\n(c) a banknote, guarantee or takaful policy; or\n\n(d) a statement, passbook or other document showing any balance in a\ncurrent, deposit or savings account.\n\nInvestment note prescribed to be securities"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  An investment note is prescribed to be  securities for the purposes of the\nsecurities laws.\n\nIslamic investment note prescribed to be Islamic securities"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4.  An Islamic investment note is prescribed to be Islamic securities for the\npurposes of the securities laws.\n\nNon-application of sections 212 and 232"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5.  Sections 212 and 232 of the Act shall not apply to an investment note and Islamic\ninvestment note that is executed or offered, on or through a recognized market.\n\nInvestment note not share, etc."
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "6.  For the purpose s of the securities laws, an investment n ote that is executed or\noffered, on or through a recognized market is not—\n\n(a) a share in , or debenture of, a body corporate or an unincorporated body;\nor\n\n(b) a unit in a unit trust scheme or prescribed investment scheme.\n\nIslamic investment note not share, etc."
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "7.  For the purpose s of the securities laws , an Islamic investment n ote that is\nexecuted or offered, on or through a recognized market is not—\n\n(a) a share in a body corporate or an unincorporated body, which are\nclassified as Shariah-compliant by the Shariah Advisory Council;\n\n(b) a unit in a unit trust  scheme or prescribed investment  scheme structured\nin compliance with Shariah principles;\n\n(c) an Islamic structured product; or\n\n(d) a sukuk structured in compliance with Shariah principles.\n\nMade 11 May 2016\n[KK/SID/P/(S)/483/669/4(SK. 8); PN(PU2)662/XI]\n\nDATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nSecond Minister of Finance"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
