 "MY-H1373": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1373",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Digital Signature (Exemption) Order\n\n (2) This Order is deemed to have come into operation on 1 January 2013.\n\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1)  The licensed certification authority  to which the Immigration\nDepartment of Malaysia is a subscriber is exempted from the requir ement under\nsubsection 59(2) of the Act in relation to a certificate issued for the purpose of verifying\nthe digital signature affixed on a passport issued under the Passports Act 1966\n[Act 150].\n\n (2) Notwithstanding subparagraph (1), the licensed certification authority\nshall not issue any certificate for the purpose of verifying the digital signature affixed on\na passport for any period exceeding six years from the date of issuance.\n\nMade 13 March 2013\n[KPKK/PUU 800-8/20; PN(PU2)575/VI]\n\nDATO' SERI UTAMA DR. RAIS BIN YATIM\nMinister of Information, Communication and Culture"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
