 "MY-H1390": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1390",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Price Control and Anti -Profiteering\n(Price Marking of Price-Controlled Goods) (No. 4) Order 2015.\n\n (2) This Order has effect for the period from 7 July 2015 to 23 July 2015.\n\nPrice marking"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) Any person who  sells or offers to sell any price -controlled goods\npublished in the Price Control and Anti-Profiteering (Determination of Maximum Price)\n(No. 5) Order 201 5 [P.U. (A) 145/2015] shall affix a pink coloured label indicating the\nprice per unit or per unit weight, the name describing such price-controlled goods and\nthe grade or quality, if any, of such price-controlled goods.\n\n (2) Any person who fails to comply with subparagraph (1 ) commits an\noffence and shall, on conviction, be liable—\n\n(a) if such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding twenty\nthousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence, to a fine\nnot exceeding fifty thousand ringgit; or\n\n(b) if such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding ten\nthousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence, to a fine\nnot exceeding twenty thousand ringgit.\n\nMade 1 July 2015\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)26/0.5001/1 Jld.12; PN(PU2)695/X]\n\nDATO' SRI HASAN BIN MALEK\nMinister of Domestic Trade,\nCo-operatives and Consumerism"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H1391": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1391",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These regulations may be cited as the Food Hygiene (Amendment)\n\nRegulations 2016.\n\n(2) These Regulations come into operation on 1 December 2016.\n\nAmendment of regulation 51"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Food Hygiene Regulations 2009 [P.U. (A) 95/2009] are amended in\n\nregulation 51—\n\n(a) by inserting after subregulation (1) the following subregulation:\n\n\"(1A) Any person who sells raw milk for direct human\n\nconsumption shall subject the milk to heat treatment—\n\n(a) by being retained at a temperature of not less than\n\n100°C for at least three minutes;\n\n(b) by being retained at a temperature of not less than\n\n135°C for at least two seconds;\n\n(c) by the Holding Method, where the temperature of\n\nthe milk is raised to not less than 63oC and not more\n\nthan 65oC and retained at not less than 63oC and not\n\nmore than 65o for at least 30 minutes and then\n\nimmediately and rapidly reduced to 4oC or less and\n\nmaintained at that temperature with protection\n\nfrom contamination until the milk is removed from\n\nthe premises for delivery; or\n\n(d) by the High Temperature Short Time Method, where\n\nthe temperature of the milk is raised to not less than\n\n73 oC and retained at the temperature for at least\n\n15 seconds or its equivalent of time and temperature\n\nrelationship and then immediately and rapidly\n\nreduced to 4oC or less and maintained at the\n\ntemperature with protection from contamination\n\nuntil the milk is removed from the premises for\n\ndelivery.\"; and\n\n(b) in subregulation (3), by inserting after the word \"(1)\" the words \", (1A)\".\n\nMade 14 April 2016\n\n[KKM-163/S/6; PN(PU2)418/XXIII]\n\nDATUK SERI DR. S. SUBRAMANIAM\n\nMinister of Health"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
