 "MY-H1503": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1503",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Stamp Duty (Exemption) Order 2020.\n\n (2) This Order is deemed to have come into operation on 27 February 2020.\n\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1)  An instrument of loan or a financing agreement relating to  the loan or\nfinancing facility executed between a small and medium enterprises  and a financial\ninstitution is, on application, exempted from stamp duty.\n\n(2) The exemption under subparagraph (1) shall apply to the said instrument\nwhich is executed pursuant to a l etter of offer issued by the financial institution on or\nafter 27 February 2020 but not later than 31 December 2020.\n\n(3) The application for an exemption under subparagraph (1) shall be\naccompanied by a letter of offer from the financial institution to the sm all and medium\nenterprises which states the approval of the loan or financing facility.\n\n(4) In this paragraph—\n\n(a) \"financial institution\" has the same meaning as that assigned to \"banker\"\nin section 2 of the Act, and any person prescribed as a financial\ninstitution by the Minister under subsection 2(1) of the Central Bank\nof Malaysia Act 2009 [Act 701]  for the purposes of section 49 of the Act;\n\n(b) \"loan or financing facility\" means a loan or financing facility approved\nunder Bank Negara Malaysia's Fund for small and medium enterprises—\n\n(i)  Special Relief Facility;\n\n(ii) All Economic Sectors Facility including Small And Medium\nEnterprises Automation and Digitalisation Facility;\n\n(iii) Agrofood Facility; or\n\n(iv) Micro Enterprises Facility; and\n\n(c) \"small and medium enterprises\" means enterprises as may be\ndetermined by the National Small and Medium Enterprises\nDevelopment Council established under section 2 A of the Small and\nMedium Industries Development Corporation Act 1995 [Act 539].\n\nMade 14 May 2020\n[MOF.TAX. 700-1/3/11 Jld.2(40); PN(PU2)159/XXXIII]\n\n                     TENGKU DATO' SRI ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\n                              Minister of Finance"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H1505": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1505",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These rules may be cited as the Employees Provident Fund\n\n(Amendment) (No. 2) Rules 2022.\n\n (2) These Rules come into operation on 1 July 2022.\n\nAmendment of rule 41"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Employees Provident Fund Rules 1991 [P.U. (A) 493/1991], which are\n\nreferred to as \"the principal Rules\" in these Rules, are amended in rule 41 by deleting\n\nsubrules (10F), (10N), (10O), (10P), (10Q), (10R), (10S), (10T), (10ZB), (10ZC), (10ZD),\n\n(10ZE), (10ZF), (10ZG), (10ZH), (10ZI), (10ZJ), (10ZK), (10ZL), (10ZM) and (10ZN).\n\nSavings"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) Any notice of withdrawal made under paragraph 54(6)(k), (l), (m) or (n) of\n\nthe Act on or before 31 March 2021, 30 June 2021, 30 September 2021 or 30 April 2022,\n\nrespectively, which is pending before the date of coming into operation of these Rules\n\nshall, on the date of coming into operation of these Rules, be dealt with in accordance\n\nwith the provisions of the principal Rules as if the principal Rules had not been amended\n\nby these Rules.\n\n(2) Any authorization, direction, decision or other executive acts made, given\n\nor done in relation to subrule (10F), (10N), (10O), (10P), (10Q), (10R), (10S), (10T), (10ZB),\n\n(10ZC), (10ZD), (10ZE), (10ZF), (10ZG), (10ZH), (10ZI), (10ZJ), (10ZK), (10ZL), (10ZM) or\n\n(10ZN) before the date of coming into operation of these Rules shall, on the date of coming\n\ninto operation of these Rules, continue in full force and effect in relation to\n\nthe member of the Fund to whom the authorization, direction, decision or other executive\n\nacts applied until amended, repealed, rescinded, revoked or replaced.\n\n(3) Any investigation or legal proceedings instituted in relation to\n\nsubrule (10F), (10N), (10O), (10P), (10Q), (10R), (10S), (10T), (10ZB), (10ZC), (10ZD),\n\n(10ZE), (10ZF), (10ZG), (10ZH), (10ZI), (10ZJ), (10ZK), (10ZL), (10ZM) or (10ZN) which is\n\npending before the date of coming into operation of these Rules shall, on the date of\n\ncoming into operation of these Rules, be continued in accordance with the provisions of\n\nthe principal Rules as if the principal Rules had not been amended by these Rules.\n\nMade 13 April 2022\n\n[MOF.SBM(R) 600-41/39/91; PN(PU2)498/Jld.19]\n\n TAN SRI AHMAD BADRI BIN MOHD ZAHIR\n\n Chairman\n\n Employees Provident Fund Board"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
