 "MY-H1633": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1633",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1)   This order may be cited as the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 2) Order 2011.\n(2) This Order is deemed to have effect from the year of assessment 2007 until the\nyear of assessment 2009.\nApplication"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. This Order applies to Islamic securities, other than convertible loan stock, which are\nissued in accordance with the princi ples of Mudharabah, Musyarakah, Ijarah, Istisna' or any\nother principle approved by the Shariah Advisory Council established by the Securities\nCommission under the Capital Markets and Services Act 2007 [Act 671].\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister exempts an in dividual, unit trust or listed close -end fund in the basis\nperiod for a year of assessment from the payment of income tax in respect of any gains or\nprofits received from the investment in Islamic securities.\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Section 109 of the Act sh all not apply to any gains or profits received by a non -\nresident individual, unit trust or listed close-end fund referred to in paragraph 3.\n\nMade 15 April 2011\n[Perb.CR(8.09)294/6/4-9(SJ.9)(2010)(SK.5);LHDN01/35/(S)/42/51/231-31;\nPN(PU2)80/LXI]\nDATO' SERI HAJI AHAMD HUSNI BIN MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nSecond Minister Of Finance\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the Income Tax Act\n1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
