 "MY-H1697": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1697",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Loans Guarantee (Bodies Corporate)\n(Remission of Tax and Stamp Duty) (No. 2) Order 2012.\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 30 May 2012.\nRemission of Tax"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. Any tax payable under the Income Tax Act 1967 [Act 53] shall be remitted in full\nin respect of any money payable under any agreement, note, instrument or document in\nrelation to any of the Islamic Medium Term Notes issued pursuant to the Islamic\nMedium Term Notes Programme in nominal val ue of three hundred thousand million\nringgit (RM3,000,000,000 .00) (\" the IMTN Programme\") by Johor Corporation (\" the\nIssuer\") including but not limited to any agreement, note, instrument and document in\nrelation to the guarantee (\" the Guarantee\") provided o r to be provided by the\nGovernment of Malaysia, which is payable by—\n(a) the I ssuer, to which this Act applies by virtue of the Loans Guarantee\n(Declaration of Bodies Corporate) (Johor Corporation) Order 2012\n[P.U. (A) 128/2012];\n(b) any resident holder of the Islamic Medium Term Notes in respect of\ninvestment income;\n(c) any non-resident holder of the Islamic Medium Term Notes in respect of\nwithholding tax; or\n\n(d) any other party to any agreement, note, instrument and document in\nrelation to the Islamic Medium Term Notes, the IMTN Programme or the\nGuarantee, including any party to whom such agreement, note,\ninstrument and document is transferred or assigned.\nRemission of stamp duty"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. Any stamp duty payable under the Stamp Act 1949 [ Act 378 ] in respect of any\nagreement, note, instrument and document in relation to the Islamic Medium Term\nNotes, the IMTN Programme or the Guarantee shall be remitted in full.\nMade 28 May 2012\n[KK/BPKA/M/(S)/689/1/1; PN(PU2)232/VII]\nDATO' SERI HAJI AHMAD HUSNI BIN MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nSecond Minister of Finance"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H1698": {
  "lawId": "MY-H1698",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Price Control and Anti -Profiteering\n(Price Marking of Price-Controlled Goods) (No. 3) Order 2013.\n\n (2) This Order has effect for the period from 27 May 2013 to 2 June 2013.\n\nPrice marking"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) Any person who  sells or offers to sell any price -controlled goods\npublished in P.U. (A) 163/2013 shall affix a pink coloured label indicating the price per\nunit or per unit weight, the name describing such goods and the grade or quality, if any,\nof such price-controlled goods.\n\n (2) Any person who fails to comply  with subparagraph (1) commits an\noffence and shall, on conviction, be liable—\n\n(a) where such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\ntwenty thousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence,\nto a fine not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit; or\n\n(b) where such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\nten thousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence, to a\nfine not exceeding twenty thousand ringgit.\n\nMade 20 May 2013\n[KPDN (PGK)(S)26/0.5001/1 Jld. 12; PN(PU2)695/III]\n\nDATO' HASAN BIN MALEK\nMinister of Domestic Trade, Co-operatives and Consumerism"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
