 "MY-H2144": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2144",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) These rules may be cited as the Rules of Court (Amendment) 2019.\n\n(2) These Rules come into operation on 15 July 2019.\n\nAmendment of Order 34"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. The Rules of Court 2012 [ P.U. (A) 205/2012 ], which are referred to as t he\n\"principal Rules\" in these Rules , are amended in Order 34 by substituting for rule 10(2)\nthe following rule:\n\n\"(2) Where subparagraph (1) (b) applies to more than one party,\nthe reports shall be disclosed by mutual exchange within the time directed\nby the Court.\".\n\nAmendment of Order 55"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  Order 55 of the principal Rules are amended—\n\n(a) in rule 4(1), by inserting after the words \"the requisite number of copies of\nthe record of appeal\" the words \"in the High Court\"; and\n\n(b) in rule 5(3), by inserting after the words \"in the High Court\" the words\n\"and serve each respondent with a copy of such record of appeal\".\n\nAmendment of Order 55A"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Order 55A of the principal Rules is amended in rule 1(4), by inserting a fter the\nwords \"the originating summons shall be served\" the words \"within the time limited for\nthe filing of the appeal\".\n\nAmendment of Order 90"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5.  Order 90 of the principal Rules are amended—\n\n(a) in rule 6—\n\n(i) in the shoulder note, by substituting for the words \"Interest on money\nlodged in court\" the words \"Money deposited in court\";\n\n(ii) by substituting for paragraph (1) the following paragraph:\n\n\"(1) Any money deposited in Court shall be held without\naccruing any interest.\";\n\n(iii) by deleting paragraph (2); and\n\n(iv) by renumbering the existing paragraph (3) as paragraph (2); and\n\n(b) by deleting rule 7.\n\nAmendment of Appendix A"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "6. Appendix A of the principal Rules is amended, in  Form 38, by substituting for the\nwords \"Order 24, rule 2 (or the order herein dated the .......... day of .......... 20 .....)\" the words\n\"the order herein dated the ...... day of ............ 20 .........\".\n\nMade 22 March 2019\n[PKPMP.BD/100-1/4/1; PN(PU2)153/XVIII]\n\nRules Committee:\n\nTAN SRI DATUK SERI PANGLIMA RICHARD MALANJUM\nChief Justice, Malaysia\n\nTAN SRI DATO' SRI AHMAD BIN HJ. MAAROP\nPresident of the Court of Appeal, Malaysia\n\nTAN SRI ZAHARAH BINTI IBRAHIM\nChief Judge of the High Court in Malaya\n\nDATUK SERI PANGLIMA DAVID WONG DAK WAH\nChief Judge of the High Court in Sabah and Sarawak\n\nDATO' AMARJEET SINGH A/L SERJIT SINGH\nOn behalf of the Attorney General, Malaysia\n\nDATO' SETIA HAJI MOHD ZAWAWI BIN SALLEH\nJudge of the Federal Court\n\nDATUK HASNAH BINTI DATO' MOHAMMED HASHIM\nJudge of the Court of Appeal\n\nDATUK HAJAH AZIZAH BINTI HJ. NAWAWI\nJudge of the High Court in Malaya\n\nTUAN RAVINTHRAN N. PARAMAGURU\nJudge of the High Court in Sabah and Sarawak\n\nTUAN AHMAD KAMAR BIN JAMALUDIN\nSenior Sessions Court Judge, Kuala Lumpur\n\nDATO' ABDUL FAREED ABDUL GAFOOR\nAdvocate, Peninsular Malaysia\n\nENCIK BRENNDON KEITH SOH\nAdvocate, Sabah\n\nENCIK RANBIR SINGH SANGHA\nAdvocate, Sarawak\n\nSubordinate Courts Rules Committee:\n\nTAN SRI DATUK SERI PANGLIMA RICHARD MALANJUM\nChief Justice, Malaysia\n\nTAN SRI DATO' SRI AHMAD BIN HJ. MAAROP\nPresident of the Court of Appeal, Malaysia\n\nTAN SRI ZAHARAH BINTI IBRAHIM\nChief Judge of the High Court in Malaya\n\nDATUK SERI PANGLIMA DAVID WONG DAK WAH\nChief Judge of the High Court in Sabah and Sarawak\n\nDATO' AMARJEET SINGH A/L SERJIT SINGH\nOn behalf of the Attorney General, Malaysia\n\nDATO' SETIA HAJI MOHD ZAWAWI BIN SALLEH\nJudge of the Federal Court\n\nDATUK HASNAH BINTI DATO' MOHAMMED HASHIM\nJudge of the Court of Appeal\n\nDATUK HAJAH AZIZAH BINTI HJ. NAWAWI\nJudge of the High Court in Malaya\n\nTUAN RAVINTHRAN N. PARAMAGURU\nJudge of the High Court in Sabah and Sarawak\n\nTUAN AHMAD KAMAR BIN JAMALUDIN\nSenior Sessions Court Judge, Kuala Lumpur\n\nDATO' ABDUL FAREED ABDUL GAFOOR\nAdvocate, Peninsular Malaysia\n\nENCIK BRENNDON KEITH SOH\nAdvocate, Sabah\n\nENCIK RANBIR SINGH SANGHA\nAdvocate, Sarawak\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 17(5) of the Courts of\nJudicature Act 1964 and section 8 of the Subordinate Courts Rules Act 1955]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H2146": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2146",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1.  (1)   This order may be cited as the  Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 3 )\nOrder 2021.\n\n(2)  This Order has effect from the year of assessment 2021.\n\nApplication"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. This Order shall apply to sukuk wakala of nominal value up to one billion and\nthree hundred million United States Dollar (US$1,300,000,000.00), other than\nconvertible loan stock , issued in accordance with the principle of Wakala by Malaysia\nWakala Sukuk Berhad.\n\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The Minister exempts any person from the payment of income tax in the\nbasis period for a  year of assessment in relation to gains or profits derived, in lieu of\ninterest, from the sukuk wakala.\n\n(2) Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or is deemed to have absolved\nthe person from complying with any requirement to submit any return or statement of\naccounts or to furnish any other information under the Act.\n\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. Section 109 of the Act shall not apply to the income exempted under this Order.\n\nMade 22 April 2021\n[MOF.TAX(S)700-3/1/547; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)–111; PN(PU2)80/C]\n\nTENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the\n Income Tax Act 1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
