 "MY-H2225": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2225",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 4)\nOrder 2021.\n\n (2) This Order  shall have effect from the year of assessment 2020 until\nthe year of assessment 2025.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order —\n\n\"qualifying person\" means a company incorporated under the\nCompanies Act 2016 [ Act 777 ], or an association or organization register ed under\nthe Societies Act 1966 [ Act 335 ], which carries on business or activity other than\nbusiness or activity of promoting and organizing conferences;\n\n \"statutory income \" means fees and other payments received by a qualifying\nperson from promoting an d organizing conferences which includes the arranging\nof accommodation, tours and sightseeing for foreign participants  derived from\norganizing conferences held in Malaysia , less allowable expenses for tax purposes and\ncapital allowance, if any; and\n\n\"foreign participants\" means individuals who are non -Malaysian citizens\nparticipating in conferences held in Malaysia, but does not include individuals\nwho are non-Malaysian citizens who reside in Malaysia.\n\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1)  The Minister exempts a qualifying person resident in Malaysia from\nthe payment of income tax in respect of the statutory income derived from organizing\nconferences held in Malaysia.\n\n (2)  The exemption in subparagraph (1) shall not apply if the total number of\nforeign participants broug ht in by that qualifying person for conferences held\nin Malaysia is less than five hundred in the basis period for a year of assessment.\n\n (3)  Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or be deemed to have absolved\nthe qualif ying person from complying w ith any requirement to submit any return\nor statement of accounts or to furnish any other information under the Act.\n\nMaintaining of separate account"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The qualifying person exempted under subparagraph 3 (1) shall maintain\na separate account for the income derived under such subparagraph.\n\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5. This Order shall not apply to a person who has been granted an exemption\nunder Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 53) Order 2000 [P.U. (A) 500/2000].\n\nMade  20 April 2021\n[MOF/TAX(S)700-1/3/5; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-106; PN(PU2)80/C]\n\nTENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
