 "MY-H2383": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2383",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Financial Services (Minimum\nAmount of Capital Funds) (Approved Person) Order 2013.\n\n (2) This Order comes into operation on 30 June 2013.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"purse limit\" means the maximum monetary value that can be stored in an\nelectronic money;\n\n\"outstanding electronic money liabilities\" means—\n\n(a) the unutili zed amount of electronic money which has been\nissued; and\n\n(b) the util ized amount of electronic money which is pending\npayment to merchants,\n\nwhere for the purpose of calculation of minimum capital fu nds, the calculation of\nthese liabilities shall be based on the monthly average of outstanding electronic\nmoney liabilities in the preceding six consecutive months;\n\n\"large electronic money scheme\" means an electronic money scheme with a\npurse limit exceeding two hundred ringgit or outstanding electronic money\nliabilities for six consecutive months amounting to one million ringgit or more;\n\n\"small electronic money scheme\" me ans an electronic money scheme with a\npurse limit not exceeding two hundred ringgit and outstanding electronic money\nliabilities of less than one million ringgit.\n\nMinimum capital funds"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) The minimum amount of capital funds of an approved person, oth er\nthan an approved insurance broker, shall be in accordance with the amount\nspecified in Schedule 1.\n\n(2) The minimum amount of capital funds of an approved insurance\nbroker shall be in accordance with the amount specified in Schedule 2.\n\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. This Order shall not apply to an approved person which is—\n\n(a)       a licensed person under the Act; and\n\n(b) a prescribed institution under the Development Financial\nInstitutions Act 2002 [Act 618].\n\nSCHEDULE 1\n\n[Subparagraph 3(1)]\n\nCategory Minimum capital funds\n(RM)\n\nApproved financial adviser 100,000\n\nApproved issuer of electronic money under—\n\n(a)   a large electronic money scheme; or\n\n(b)   a small electronic money scheme\n\n5,000,000 or 8% of its\noutstanding electronic\nmoney liabilities,\nwhichever is higher\n\n100,000\n\nApproved money broker\n\n200,000\n\nSCHEDULE 2\n\n[Subparagraph 3(2)]\n\nPeriod Until\n30 December 2013\nOn and after\n31 December 2013\nOn and after\n31 December 2014\n\nMinimum capital\nfunds (RM)\n\n500,000 750,000 1,000,000\n\nMade 19 June 2013\n[BNM/JUN/1125/50/01; PN(PU2) 718]\n\nTAN SRI DATO' SRI DR. ZETI AKHTAR AZIZ\n                         Governor\n                       Central Bank of Malaysia"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
