 "MY-H2948": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2948",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1.  (1)  These regulations may be cited as the Income Tax (Special Treatment\nfor Interest on Loan) Regulations 2020.\n\n(2)  These Regulations shall have effect for the  year of assessment 2020\nand subsequent years of assessment.\n\nApplication"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  These Regulations apply to—\n\n(a) the following banks:\n\n(i) a licensed bank or licensed investment bank under the\nFinancial Services Act 2013 [Act 758]; and\n\n(ii) a licensed Islamic bank under the Islamic Financial Services\nAct 2013 [Act 759]; and\n\n(b) a development financial institution prescribed under the\nDevelopment Financial Institutions Act 2002 [Act 618];\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3.  In these Regulations—\n\n\"small and medium enterprises\" has the same meaning assigned to it\nunder section 2 of the Small and Medium Industries Development\nCorporation Act 1995 [Act 539];\n\n\"loan\" means any loan or financing which is related to the moratorium programme\nunder the Prihatin Rakyat Economic Stimulus Package (PRIHATIN), granted by a bank or\nfinancial institution to an individual,   small and medium enterprises or any company\nother than small and medium enterprises, but does not include credit card facility.\n\nGross income of bank and financial institution"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4.  (1)  Subject to the conditions in regulation 5, where a moratorium is approved\nby a bank or financial institution  in respect of any amount of interest on a loan which is\ndue and payable from 1 April 2020 until 30 September 2020 in the basis period for a year\nof assessment, such interest shall not constitute the gross income of that bank or financial\ninstitution in the basis period for that year of assessment.\n\n(2)  Notwithstanding subregulation (1), where any amount of interest\non a loan—\n\n(a) is received from 1 April 2020 until 30 September 2020; or\n\n(b) becomes receivable on or after 1 October 2020,\n\nby the bank or financial institution in the basis period for a year of assessment, such\ninterest shall be treated as the gross income of the bank or financial institution in the\nbasis period for that year of assessment.\n\nConditions relating to loan and moratorium"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5. The following conditions shall apply relating to a loan and moratorium:\n\n(a) the loan is in ringgit;\n\n(b) there is no outstanding payment on the lo an for more than ninety days\nas at 1 April 2020; and\n\n(c) relating to a company other than a small and medium enterprise,\nthe application for the moratorium has been made to the relevant bank\nor financial institution.\n\nLoan impairment"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "6. A deduction from the gross income of a bank or financial institution based on any\nimpairment of a loan shall not be allowed.\n\nSeparate account"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "7.  The bank and financial institution shall maintain a separate account,\nfor the amount of interest referred to in subregulation  4(1) and payment received\nin relation to that interest, and the amount of interest received and becomes receivable\nunder subregulation 4(2).\n\nMade 24 August 2020\n[Perb.MOF.TAX(RB)700-2/1/89; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-36; PN(PU2)80/XCIX]\n\n            DATO' SRI DR. SABIN BIN SAMITAH\nDirector General of Inland Revenue"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
 "MY-H2949": {
  "lawId": "MY-H2949",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Price Control and Anti -Profiteering\n(Price Marking of Price-Controlled Goods) (No. 4) Order 2021.\n\n (2) This Order has effect for the period from 27 May 2021 to 2 June 2021.\n\nPrice marking"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. (1) Any person who sells or offers to sell any price-controlled goods published\nin the Price Control and Anti -Profiteering (Determination of Maximum Price) (No. 4)\nOrder 2021  [P.U. (A) 236/2021 ] shall affix a pink coloured label indicating\nthe price per unit or per unit weight, the name describing such price -controlled goods\nand the grade or quality, if any, of such price-controlled goods.\n\n (2) Any person who fails to comply with subparagraph (1) commits\nan offence and shall, on conviction, be liable—\n\n(a) if such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\ntwenty thousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence, to\na fine not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit; or\n\n(b) if such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\nten thousand ringgit and, for a second or subsequent offence,\nto a fine not exceeding twenty thousand ringgit.\n\nMade 11 May 2021\n[KPDN(PGK)(S)26/0.5001/1 Jld.12; PN(PU2)695/Jld. 29]\n\n                                                                               DATO SRI ALEXANDER NANTA LINGGI\nMinister of Domestic Trade and Consumer Affairs"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
