 "MY-H3024": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3024",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may b e cited as the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 6) Order\n(2) This Order is shall have effect from the year of assessment 2012.\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\"non-resident person\" means a related company of the treasury management\ncentre or a financial institution who is not resident in Malaysia within the meaning of\nsection 8 of the Act;\n\"treasury management centre\" means  a company which is—\n(a) incorporated under the Companies Act 1965 [ Act 125 ] and resident in\nMalaysia;\n(b) carrying on a business of providing qualifying services in Malaysia as\nspecified by the Minister;\n(c) approved by the Minister upon fulfilling the conditions specified by him.\n\"related company\" has the same meaning as defined under section 2 of the\nPromotion of Investments Act 1986 [Act 327];\n\n\"exempt years of assessment\" means five consecutive years of assessment where\nthe statutory income of a treasury management centre is exempt from income tax\nunder the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 5) 2012 in relation to its business of providing\nqualifying services.\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. The Minister exempts a non -resident person from the payment of income tax in\nrespect of interest on borrowings to the treasury management centre for the purpose of\nproviding qualifying services by that centre during the exempt years of assessment.\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The provisions of section 109 of the Act shall not apply to the income exempted\nunder this Order.\nMade 30 July 2012\n[Perb. (SK.); LHDN. 01/35/(S)/42/51/231-7.13; PN(PU2)80/LXIV]\nDATO' SERI AHMAD HUSNI BIN MOHAMAD HANADZLAH\nSecond Minister of Finance\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 127(4) of the Income Tax Act\n1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
