 "MY-H3270": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3270",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. Premis kerajaan\n\nMana-mana hospital dan klinik kesihatan yang memenuhi kritera bagi\n\nmaksud latihan sebagaimana yang dinyatakan oleh Lembaga Farmasi dan\n\nmendapat kelulusannya."
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. Premis bukan kerajaan\n\nMana-mana hospital swasta, pengilang farmaseutikal, farmasi runcit dan\n\ninstitusi pendidikan tinggi yang memenuhi kritera bagi maksud latihan\n\nsebagaimana yang dinyatakan oleh Lembaga Farmasi dan mendapat\n\nkelulusannya.\".\n\nDibuat 24 Julai 2012\n\n[KK(R)608(16); PN(PU2)200/III]\n\n DATO' SRI LIOW TIONG LAI\n\n Menteri Kesihatan\n\nREGISTRATION OF PHARMACISTS ACT 1951\n\nREGISTRATION OF PHARMACISTS (AMENDMENT OF SECOND SCHEDULE) ORDER\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 6A(5) of the Registration of\n\nPharmacists Act 1951 [Act 371], the Minister, after consulting the Board, makes the\n\nfollowing order:\n\nCitation\n\n1. This order may be cited as the Registration of Pharmacists (Amendment of\n\nSecond Schedule) Order 2012.\n\nAmendment of the Second Schedule\n\n2. The Registration of Pharmacists Act 1951 [Act 371] is amended by substituting\n\nfor the Second Schedule the following schedule:\n\n\"SECOND SCHEDULE\n\n[Subsection 6A(2)]\n\nLIST OF PREMISES\n\n1. Government premises\n\nAny hospital and health clinic which fulfil the criteria for the purpose of\n\ntraining as specified by the Pharmacy Board and obtain its approval.\n\n2. Non-governmental premises\n\nAny private hospital, pharmaceutical manufacturer, retail pharmacy and\n\nhigher educational institution which fulfil the criteria for the purpose of\n\ntraining as specified by the Pharmacy Board and obtain its approval. \".\n\nMade 24 July 2012\n\n[KK(R)608(16); PN(PU2)200/III]\n\n DATO' SRI LIOW TIONG LAI\n\n Minister of Health"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
