 "MY-H3603": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3603",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1.  (1)  These rules may be cited as the Income Tax (Capital Allowance)\n(Development Cost for Customised Computer Software) Rules 2019.\n\n(2)  These Rules shall have effect from the year of assessment 2018.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2.  In these Rules, \"development cost for customised computer software\" means\nconsultation fee, payment for rig hts of software ownership and incidental fee relating\nto the development of customised computer software.\n\nApplication"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1) These Rules shall apply to a resident in Malaysia, in respect of\ndevelopment cost for customised computer software incurred by the person in the basis\nperiod for a year of assessment from the year of assessment 2018.\n\n (2) For the purpose of these Rules, the development cost for customised\ncomputer software incurred in the basis period for a year of assessment or relevant\nyears of assessment shall be deemed to be incurred by the person in the basis period for\na year of assessment on which the customised computer software is capable of being\nused for the purpose of his business.\n\nInitial allowance"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The person referred to in rule 3 qualifies for an initial allowance which shall be\nequal to one fifth of the development cost for customised computer software incurred.\n\nAnnual allowance"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 5,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 5"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "5. The person referred to in rule 3 qualifies for an annual allowance which shall be\nequal to one fifth of the development cost for customised computer software incurred.\n\nNon-application"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 6,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 6"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "6. These Rules shall not apply to a person who has incurred the development cost\nfor customised computer software  for a basis period for a year of assessment wh ere\nduring that basis period the person is eligible and has claimed , in respect of that\ncustomised computer software—\n\n(a) any incentive under the Promotion of Investments Act 1986 [Act 327];\n\n(b) any deduction under section 33 of the Act;\n\n(c) any deduction under section 34A of the Act;\n\n(d) reinvestment allowance under Schedule 7A to the Act;\n\n(e) investment allowance for service sector under Schedule 7B to the Act;\n\n(f) accelerated capital allowance under any rules made under section 154 of\nthe Act; or\n\n(g) tax exemption under para graph 127(3) (b) or subsection 127(3 A) of the\nAct in respect of his statutory income which is equivalent to any part or\nthe whole of the amount of the development cost for customised\ncomputer software incurred by the person.\n\nRevocation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 7,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 7"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "7. The Income Tax (D eduction for Information Technology -Related Expenditure)\nRules 2000 [ P.U. (A) 51/2000 ] are revoked with effect from the year of\nassessment 2018.\n\nMade 27 September 2019\n[Perb. CR(8.09)681/2-61(SJ.18)JLD.14(SK.9)]; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-3(Jld.2);\nPN(PU2)80/XCVI]\n\nLIM GUAN ENG\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuant to subsection 154(2) of\nthe Income Tax Act 1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
