 "MY-H3748": {
  "lawId": "MY-H3748",
  "sourceLang": "ms",
  "targetLang": "en",
  "engine": "official-extract",
  "model": null,
  "promptVersion": null,
  "translatedAt": "2026-10-28",
  "reviewed": "official",
  "note": "公报原生英文版（与马来文版同一公报并置），逐字照录，非机译；2026-10-28 自 OCR 阶段产物回填（首轮分卷覆盖丢失）。",
  "articles": [
   {
    "no": 1,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 1"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "1. (1) This order may be cited as the Income Tax (Exemption) (No. 6)\nOrder 2021.\n\n(2) This Order has effect from the year of assessment 2021 until\nthe year of assessment 2023.\n\nInterpretation"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 2,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 2"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "2. In this Order—\n\n\"Securities Commission Malaysia\" means the Securities Commission Malaysia\nestablished under section 3 of the Securities Commission Malaysia Act 1993 [Act 498];\n\n \"qualifying company\" means a company which—\n\n(a)  is incorporated under the Companies Act 2016 [Act 777];\n\n(b)  is resident in Malaysia; and\n\n(c) holds a Capital Markets Services Licence under the Capital Markets and\nServices Act 2007 [ Act 671 ] to carry on the business referred to\nin subparagraph 3(1).\n\nExemption"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 3,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 3"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "3. (1)  The Minister exempts a qualifying company from the payment\nof income tax in a basis period for a year of assessment in respect of the statutory income\nderived from a business of provid ing fund management services  to business trust or\nreal estate investment trust in Malaysia.\n\n(2) An exemption granted under subparagraph (1) shall be subject to the\nqualifying company obtaining annual certif ication from the Securities Commission\nMalaysia that the following conditions have been fulfilled  namely the\nqualifying company—\n\n(a) provides fund management services to business trust\nor real estate investment trust in Malaysia in accordance with\nShariah principles;\n\n(b) has at least two full -time employees in Malaysia of which\none of the employees holds a Capital Markets Services\nRepresentative's Licence under the Capita l Markets and Services\nAct 2007; and\n\n(c) incurs annual operating expenditure of at least two hundred and\nfifty thousand ringgit (RM250,000.00) in Malaysia.\n\n(3) For the purposes of subparagraph (1)—\n\n(a) \"fund management \" has the same meaning assi gned to it\n  in the Capital Markets and Services Act 2007;\n\n(b) \"business trust \" has the same meaning assi gned to it  in the\n  Capital Markets and Services Act 2007; and\n\n(c) \"real estate investment trust\" has the same meaning as provided\n  in the guideline s relating to real  estate investment trust issued\n  by the Securities Commission Malaysia under the\n  Capital Markets and Services Act 2007.\n\n(4)  Nothing in subparagraph (1) shall absolve or be deemed to have absolved\nthe qualifying company from complying with any requirement to submit any return or\nstatement of accounts or to furnish any other information under the Act.\n\nSeparate account"
    }
   },
   {
    "no": 4,
    "noLabel": {
     "en": "Section 4"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "4. The qualifying company shall maintain a separate account for the income\nderived from the business referred to in subparagraph 3(1) in the basis period for\neach year of assessment and that income shall be treated as a separate and distinct\nsource of business for the qualifying company.\n\nMade 25 June 2021\n[Perb. MOF.TAX(S) 700-3/1/613; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-73; PN(PU2)/80 Jld. 101]\n\n   TENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\nMinister of Finance\n\n[To be laid before the Dewan Rakyat pursuan t to subsection 127(4) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967]"
    }
   }
  ]
 },
